TITLE:: CollapseButton
summary:: A button for the CollapseView
categories:: GUI>Views, Libraries>jostMlib
related:: jostMlib,  Classes/CollapseView


NOTE::
Not meant for direct instantiation, unless you know what you are doing.
Using CollapseView is recommended.

However if you do use CollapseButton, you can instantly convert a FlowView into a CollapseView,
but you must watch out for the warnings below.

NOTE THE DOUBLE LAYER OF FLOW VIEWS!
::

CLASSMETHODS::
METHOD:: clickModifier
default 524288 ("option" key  on macos)

PRIVATE:: viewClass
PRIVATE:: new

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: value
the button value

METHOD:: parent
PRIVATE:: storeBounds
METHOD:: minHeight
The collapsed height. the default is CollapseView.defaultMinHeight (25).
METHOD:: offset


PRIVATE:: drawFunction
PRIVATE:: collapseFunction

METHOD:: valueAction
set 1 or zero to collaps or expand the view
METHOD:: color
PRIVATE:: init
METHOD:: eq
boolean. default false. Use equilateral triangle
METHOD:: scale
scale the triangle in the button rect. default=0.5;

EXAMPLES::
code::
(
FlowView(bounds:Window.flipY(Rect(300,200,400,600))).flow{|w|
	3.do{arg i;var cb;
		FlowView(w,Rect(0,0,300,300))
		.flow{|w|
			w.flow{arg w; // NOTE THE DOUBLE LAYER OF FLOW VIEWS. This is mandatory for the CollapseButton to work.
				cb= CollapseButton(w).offset_(4); // prevent hiding the first 4 items (including arrow).
				Button.new(w,Rect(0,0,50,25)).states_([["Start"]]);
				Button.new(w,Rect(0,0,50,25)).states_([["Pause"]]);
				Button.new(w,Rect(0,0,50,25)).states_([["Stop"]]);
				w.startRow;
				7.do{|i|
					EZSlider.new(w,Rect(0,0,270,20), "slider"+i);
				};
			}
		};
		cb.valueAction_(i-1); // converts to boolean.  collapse the first two.
		// You must call button AFTER running .flow
	};


}
)

::

